  "worked_solution": "The speed is $660$ meters per minute. To find the time it took the jet ski to cover $3\\,960$ meters, we divide the distance by $660.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,960}{660} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,960\u00f760}{660\u00f760} \\\\  & =\\frac{66}{11} \\\\  & =66\u00f711 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the jet ski was in motion for $6$ minutes.",
